@startuml <SLUG>_BDD
' =====================================================================
' Block Definition Diagram (BDD) — STARTER TEMPLATE  (Phase 03, diagram 2 of 7)
' Builds on: System decomposition from SyRS §2 System Overview.
' Conventions §7. Replace <PLACEHOLDERS>; delete (example) lines. Keep <=12 blocks/diagram —
' split into per-subsystem BDDs if larger. The BDD is a LIVING document (sharpens at IBD/ICD).
' Connector meaning (decide deliberately):
'   *--  composition  (part CANNOT exist without the whole; whole owns lifecycle)
'   o--  aggregation  (shared part, independent lifecycle — open diamond; never call it "composes")
'   --   association  (loose "uses/has-a", no ownership)
'   <|-- generalization (sub-type IS-A super-type)
' =====================================================================
title <Project Name> — Block Definition Diagram (TODO)

class "<System (top-level block)>" as System <<block>> {
  + <valueProperty> : <Type>
  + <operation>() : <ReturnType>
}

class "<Sub-block A>" as SubA <<block>> {
  + <attr> : <Type>
  + <op>() : <Type>
}
class "<Sub-block B>" as SubB <<block>> {
  + <attr> : <Type>
}
class "<Sub-block C>" as SubC <<block>> {
  + <attr> : <Type>
}
' class "Controller" as Ctrl <<block>> { + state : Mode }   ' (example — delete)

' --- Structural connectors (pick the right one per pair) ---
System *-- SubA : <<composition>>
System o-- SubB : <<aggregation>>
System --  SubC : <<association>>

' --- Generalization example (delete if unused) ---
' class "<Specialized Block>" as Spec <<block>>
' SubA <|-- Spec

' --- Satisfy assertions (a block satisfies a REQ — assertion, NOT proof) ---
note bottom of SubA
  satisfies REQ-<id>
  TODO: list REQs each block satisfies (mirror into Model_Coverage_Matrix.md)
end note

@enduml
